      "message": "For the intended use in chrome, will it always just be 0,1, or 2 filters (no image filter, regular image filter, and the drop shadow compositing)?\n\nIf that\u0027s the case, I\u0027m fine imposing a limit, since anything beyond a low N will just take forever to render anyways. If there is user-provided content that can list an arbitrary number of filters, then we should push back against the spec.\n\nWe could just update our fuzzer to limit the N it chooses; chrome\u0027s saveLayer parsing is handled separately so a compromised renderer process shouldn\u0027t be able to exploit it anyways.",
